          "title": "Chrononauts",
          "subtitle": "Vying",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Chrononauts is a commercial time-travel card game where players alter a timeline to satisfy identity and mission goals."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Published by Looney Labs in 2000, Chrononauts uses a card tableau timeline and hand-management effects to create time-travel paradoxes and alternate histories."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "title": "Setup",
          "subtitle": "Table, deck, equipment, and deal",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "1-6 players use the table arrangement described for Chrononauts."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Dedicated Chrononauts timeline, action, ID, and mission cards"
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Dedicated Chrononauts timeline, action, ID, and mission cards, score area, and enough table space for play."
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "text": "Lay out the timeline cards and deal each player identity, mission, and hand cards from the dedicated deck."
